confusb (0.2.3-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * New "Configuration" tab: it tells whether a device can be configured
    (Configurable, Maybe configurable, System settings, Not configurable)
    and why, from its HID report descriptor (a manufacturer-specific channel
    of feature or output reports), the camera (V4L2) and audio (ALSA)
    controls with their current values, the devices supported by libratbag,
    Solaar and OpenRazer (tables included, generated by
    tools/generar_soporte.py from the Debian packages) and the system
    settings. It lists the tools that help and whether they are installed.
    Each card of the device list shows the verdict.
  * 69 new strings, translated into all the languages.

 -- masebastia <msebastia@protonmail.com>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:46:47 +0100

confusb (0.2.2-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * The window starts the user service if it is enabled but not running
    (right after installing the package it only starts at the next login).
  * Probes: for an Android phone with USB debugging enabled and authorized,
    read through adb the commercial name, model, Android version, security
    patch, processor, memory, screen, battery and storage; show the storage
    of a phone already mounted over MTP; add the full udev attribute tree
    for any device. adb is now suggested, and the adb server is stopped
    again if the probe had to start it.
  * Interface: choose the window background, either the circuit-board image
    or a solid color; with a solid color the light or dark theme is chosen
    so that everything stays readable.
  * 51 new strings, translated into all the languages.

 -- masebastia <msebastia@protonmail.com>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:52:51 +0100

confusb (0.2.1-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Connection policy: only the active session reacts (with several users
    logged in), devices that are already known are not offered again, a
    device seen for the first time is offered with a notification ("View
    information" button) and storage drives are opened with the default
    application once mounted (unless GNOME already does it).
  * Show the capacity, partitions and file systems of storage drives.
  * New "Notices" card in the window with the pending offers; opening the
    window withdraws the notifications and the counter on the icon.
  * Split the service and the window into two processes: the service no
    longer loads GTK (about 30 MB instead of 300 MB) and the window leaves
    the memory when it is closed. The service has its own application ID and
    a hidden desktop file (es.masebastia.confusb.servicio.desktop) for its
    notifications. After upgrading, restart the user service:
    systemctl --user restart confusb.service
  * Fix the "About" dialog (the Close button did not respond, the panel was
    cut off), fit the glass dialogs to short windows and keep every vertical
    scrollbar off the content.
  * Raw data boxes: line spacing, horizontal scrollbar, minimum window width.
  * 23 new strings, translated into all the languages.
  * Build-Depends: add the GObject introspection packages used by the tests.

 -- masebastia <msebastia@protonmail.com>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:03:02 +0100

